92186045417] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1045 "Surface Integrals Over Cartesian Surfaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "55efdebf-c5f4-5896-8a96-24cfe4c710eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106060 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186102246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106060 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161106" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106060 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the surface integral of the function $f(x, y, z) = 2xy$, where the surface $S$ is defined by $z = x^{2} + y^{2}$ for $-1 \\le x \\le 1$ and $0 \\le y \\le 2$.\nThis surface integral can be written as a repeated integral, as shown below.\n$∬_(S)f(x, y, z)dS = \\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^{1}\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2}AAAAAAAdydx$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106060 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7f27ceb2-3e83-5aa6-8caa-7e1929889c49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1061 44418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f07960b-27be-5aa0-93a1-7182414f7f51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1061 44419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a2865c0f-bb8c-5298-b8b6-d39fcd4dd416" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1061 44421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4324e02b-29a0-51f1-961f-3fecc2a25950" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1061 44429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "edfeb55c-dcca-540f-9b5b-f35820d75f59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that for a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNow, if a surface is given by the explicit equation $z=g(x,y)$ over a plane region $D$ in Cartesian coordinates, then the canonical parametrization of this surface is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,y) = \\langle x,\\:  y, \\: g(x,y) \\rangle, \\qquad (x,y) \\in D.\n$$\n\nMoreover, we know that under the canonical parametrization, the magnitude of the fundamental vector product is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{x}^{'}\\times {r}_{y}^{'}‖ & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f\\left(x,y,g(x,y)\\right) \\sqrt{1+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2} \\: \\text{d}A.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1065 7650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "411ccf43-163d-53bb-b1f4-2b6832c905e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
